buffer_cache: EDEN_NX2_KEEP_CPU_WRITES=1 stops downloads landing on newer CPU writes

Port of Djihads80/Eglantine fe2cd8be2b (Duck912, cherry-picked from e27fbc6b03, branch
fix/oot-blackscreen, 2026-11-05). GPL-3.0-or-later, as the core.

The source commit: with asynchronous GPU emulation Ocarina's Z-target reticle jumped back and forth.
The game writes per-frame emitter constants into double-buffered slots of a buffer the GPU also
writes. CPU writes into GPU-written memory are only collected; the GPU thread applies them later. Two
download paths wrote the GPU's older copy over them: the fencing thread's async downloads, and
WriteMemory downloading the rest of a page while the collected writes were applied one by one.
Measured there: reticle flips in 0% of frames, was 56-67%.

- Each write of downloaded data to guest memory skips writes collected and not yet applied
  (GPUDirtyMemoryManager::ForEachPending reads them without consuming them).
- InvalidateGPUCache hands the writes over as one batch; the Vulkan rasterizer takes them all out of
  the GPU-written ranges before applying any.

Changed from the source:
- Behind EDEN_NX2_KEEP_CPU_WRITES=1. Unset, no source of pending writes is set, every Intersects is
  false and InvalidateGPUCache runs its old loop. What stays is one empty RangeSet per download.
- Also covers this tree's own download sites: DownloadRangesMemory (0082) and FinishDownloadPieces
  (the small-buffer path).
- Gather is left as it is, not refactored, so frizti-v2-05 stacks beside this. nemyu-02's gather
  still applies its writes one at a time, without the claim.
- The source's buffer.Mapped() download path is left out: not part of the fix, and Buffer has no
  Mapped() here.

Locks: ForEachPending takes the manager's guard under buffer_cache.mutex. Gather holds guard only for
its swap, and frizti-v2-05's lock is a separate mutex. Read, not run.

Runs on the PS5: same core path. Pool memory: a short list per download, freed at once, switch on.
Cost: one copy of the pending lists per fence pop, switch on.

Co-authored-by: Duck912 <350528965+Duck912@users.noreply.github.com>

